00:21:50,400 --> 00:23:52,570
Thank you for watching this first episode. I will often put notes at the end of episodes to explain cultivation concepts and to detail things that might not have been adapted correctly.\N\NFirst, what is the Dao ? It's the metaphysical representation of everything in Daoism. Everything is the Dao and the Dao is everything, it's the fundamental force of the world. In a cultivation context the Dao will be used in this meaning but also used with the meaning of a path. "The Dao of alchemy" for example is the path of alchemy, the truth of alchemy, someone's understanding of what the essence of alchemy is. Pursuing the Dao is trying to understand the heavens and the earth.\N\NA common concept is "Tian Dao", the Dao of the heavens. I will be referring to it as "the law of the heavens" for simplicity's sake but you can have the double interpretation of it thanks to the understanding of what Dao means.\N\NSecond, you were introduced to cultivation levels in the character cards of this episode, the concept of what cultivation is will be further explained in the next episode so don't worry about it for now. By the way, don't hesitate to pause to read character cards.\N\NThird, you were introduced to the concept of formations with the "Fog Concealment Formation", think of formations as spells that use something as a proxy. A mountain can be used as a formation to create fog or create a barrier for example. A formation can be engraved in a plate or a stone platform, can be quickly created by planting flags in the ground, a group of people can be used as a formation, etc... You will have the occasion of seeing many formations in this story.

